<title>UK: Rolls sees $50 mln from new Emirates deal.</title>
<headline>Rolls sees $50 mln from new Emirates deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Rolls-Royce Plc said on Friday it would receive about $50 million as a result of Emirates' airline's decision to buy two more Boeing Co 777 aircraft.</p>
<p>The airline said on Thursday it planned to execute an option to buy the planes, which will be powered by Rolls-Royce's Trent 892 engines, in addition to the seven planes it had already ordered.</p>
<p>Emirates still has an option for another five 777s under a previous agreement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
